NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5002
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# ── The onboarding / portal API (mbp-backend) ────────────────────────────────
#
# Two variables, and they do different jobs. Both are read at build time, so a change needs
# a dev-server restart or a rebuild.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_MODE=live is the switch that moves the *gym* side off fixtures and off
# Supabase Auth: the onboarding wizard, the portal snapshot and the gym login all follow it
# (see client/src/lib/onboardingApi.ts). Leave it unset and the gym pages run on the demo
# fixture, which is what the marketing site wants. The admin pages under /admin ignore it
# entirely — there is no fixture admin, so they are always live.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_URL points at a stage. Unset means https://api.muscleboxpro.com, and
# that default is load-bearing in three places at once: it is the origin allowed in
# connect-src, it is the host that makes the session cookies same-site, and it is the host
# on which the sandbox bearer hatch refuses to operate. Setting it to an execute-api URL
# turns all three on together, deliberately — see rule 4 in client/src/lib/apiClient.ts.
#
# Note the stage is part of the path: .../sandbox, with no trailing slash. Dropping the
# stage answers 403 "Missing Authentication Token", which does not look like the mistake
# it is.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_MODE=live
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_URL=https://6t9q5v5v97.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sandbox
